hi here is mathias from datatab and in  this video i'd like to show you  how you can easily calculate the man  with new test  online with datatab if you want to use  your own data  you first need to clear the table  afterwards you can enter  your own data i will simply copy the  data  from the example so i copy this data  and paste it into this table  so i have two variables the reaction  time  woman and the reaction time man  in order to calculate the man with new  test i simply  click on t-test keycard r test and anova  and then select the two variables  reaction time woman and reaction time  man  now i have to choose whether i have an  independent sample  or paired sample in this case we have  independent  samples and i have to choose if i want  to calculate  a paired a parametric test or  non-parametric test  in this case we want to calculate a  non-parametric  test and now i get the results for the  men  whitney u test in this table i get the  ranks  for the two variables i get the mean  rank  and the sum of the ranks and in this  table i get the statistics for the men  with new test  so in this case i get a p-value  of 0.862 which is higher  than the p-value of 0.05  and thus and this test is not  significant  and there's no difference between  the two groups thank you for watching  this video  and if you have questions just leave me  a comment  bye
 

